    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d717">

                <pb facs="0684" n="672" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg672"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.9411/66a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-11-07T20:00:00-05:00">November 7, 1940—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>453. The American Legation at Tehran telegraphs under date November 6<anchor
                        n="94" xml:id="d717-f1"/> that according to a Soviet source Japan and Russia
                    are about to conclude some kind of agreement regarding respective spheres of
                    influence in eastern Asia.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
